## Biographies
Dr. Tasha L. Drake is a University of Chicago Provost Postdoctoral Scholar in the Lin group. She earned her Ph.D. from Northwestern University under the supervision of Peter Stair and received her B.A. in Chemistry from Amherst College in 2009. Her research interests include computational modeling of catalytic reactions within MOFs.
Pengfei Ji is a graduate student in the Lin group at the University of Chicago. He received his B.A. in Chemistry from Sichuan University in China in 2014. His research interests focus on the design, synthesis, and characterization of novel MOF catalysts for application in organic synthesis.
Prof. Wenbin Lin is the James Franck Professor of Chemistry, Radiation and Cellular Oncology, and Ludwig Center for Metastasis Research at the University of Chicago. His group has pioneered the application of MOFs in cancer therapy, bioimaging, earth-abundantmetal catalysis, artificial photosynthesis, asymmetric catalysis, and second-order nonlinear optics.
